// __ablaRuntimeHostCollectionSweep, handing what it frees to the helper.
// ---- Parallel sweep (ABLA_GC_WORKERS=n, with the parallel mark; the background-free collection only) ----------------------
// __ablaRuntimeHostBackgroundSweep on n threads, in four passes over the registry in n slices (one thread each, the collecting thread
// one of them), so that the pause has no serial walk of the registry. The collection's worklist (allocation count words, dead once the
// mark is done) is the scratch array: no second array is allocated.
//  1 (parallel): for each entry, the header's state tells garbage from kept. Garbage is poisoned (stress), its size counted, and either
//    pushed on the worker's own small-block lists (what __ablaRuntimeHostBlockKept would keep; the lists are spliced into the global
//    ones afterwards) and its slot zeroed, or tagged (the entry's bit 1) for the helper. Kept: the mark is cleared (state - 32). Each
//    worker counts its kept and tagged entries.
//  (serial, n steps) the counts give each slice its place in the dense registry (kept entries) and in the scratch array's tagged part.
//  3 (parallel, no header is read of a tagged entry): the slice's kept entries go to the scratch array, in order, at their place, and each
//    kept payload receives its new slot and unmarked state; tagged native block addresses go to the scratch array after the
//    kept ones.
//  4 (parallel, n slices of the dense registry): the kept entries are copied from the scratch array to the registry.
//  (serial) the tagged entries are appended to the helper's batch.
// Nothing in a worker allocates, takes a lock or touches thread-local storage.
// A worker's block: +0 the slice's first slot, +8 its end, +16 the garbage bytes it freed, +24 the small-block bytes it kept on
// its lists, +32 their budget, +40 its pthread handle, +48 1 once its thread started; the lists' heads follow at +64 (offset
// by block size, 65 words), then their tails at +64 + 520, then +1104 the slice's kept entries, +1112 its tagged ones, +1120 the scratch
// index of its first kept entry and +1128 of its first tagged one.
val __ablaRuntimeHostSweepBlock: int = 64 + 520 + 520 + 32

// Static: +0 the pass (1, 3 or 4), +8 whether garbage is poisoned, +16 the scratch array, +24 the kept entries in all (where the tagged
// ones start in it).
private trusted fun __ablaRuntimeHostSweepShared(): int = nativeStaticAllocate(32)

private trusted fun __ablaRuntimeHostSweepPassA(context: int): void {
